## Overview

Manually screening job applications is slow and inconsistent — recruiters spend significant time reading resumes, extracting skills, and judging fit, with no fixed rubric and no structured audit trail.

This project automates that pipeline end-to-end:

**Form submission → validation → AI skills scoring → rule-based cross-check → human review → decision routing → candidate notification → database update**

The core design principle: **AI is used only where reasoning and judgment are genuinely needed.** Everything else — validation, storage, routing, notification — is deterministic. And no candidate is ever finally shortlisted or rejected without an explicit human decision, even when the AI is confident.

## Architecture

![Architecture Diagram](./docs/Architecture-Diagram.png)

Seven stages carry a candidate from submission to a recorded, human-approved outcome. Teal stages are AI-driven; every other stage is deterministic.

Full breakdown of components, integrations, and design rationale: [`docs/Component-Credentials-List.docx`](./docs/Component-Credentials-List.docx)

## Technologies

| Layer | Technology | Role |
|---|---|---|
| Orchestration | [n8n](https://n8n.io) (self-hosted) | Form Trigger, Code, If, Switch, Wait, Postgres, Send Email nodes |
| AI / LLM | Google Gemini | Skills extraction, fit scoring, structured reasoning |
| Data storage | Supabase (Postgres) | Candidate records, scores, decisions, full audit trail |
| Notifications | Gmail SMTP | Recruiter approval email + candidate outcome email |

